DOCS = {
'docs/2002-resilio-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-exclusive-successor-control-and-split-world-fragmentation-evaluation.md': "# Resilio remedy hardening attestation predecessor authority retirement, exclusive successor control, and split-world fragmentation evaluation\n\n## What current Resilio gets right\n\nCurrent official Resilio materials still deserve credit for acknowledging several ingredients of old-world retirement, even if they do not yet elevate them into one typed control verdict.\nThat is useful.\n\nThe strongest present ingredients are:\n\n- current `Key structure and flow` docs still say changing a Standard-folder key is not distributed automatically and that peers with the old Key continue syncing with each other while no longer syncing with the peer who changed the Key\n- current `What's the difference between Standard and Advanced folders?` docs still say Standard-folder peers can share the key they have without limitation, that on-the-fly permission changes are unavailable there, and that revoke access from remote peers is only available for Advanced folders\n- current `User Management` docs still say only Owners can revoke access rights from other peers and that this permission model applies only to Advanced folders\n- current `Sync Private Identity & Linking My Devices` docs still say you cannot remotely unlink other devices\n- current `Disconnecting and Removing Folders` docs still say removing a folder from linked devices may still leave it available on remote devices that are not linked to your personal identity\n- current `Sharing single file` docs still say recipients can share files further\n- current `Can Resilio team see and block/remove any Sync folders?` docs still say Resilio cannot control link or folder distribution and cannot remove content from users' devices or their peers' devices\n- current `If your device is stolen` docs still say the serious response path is to remove shares, unlink identity if linked, remove synced data from storage, reinstall, regenerate identity, relink devices, and reshare folders\n- current `Sync Service Troubleshooting on Windows` docs still say switching to Local System creates a new storage folder where seeing no old folders is expected and operators must re-add and re-share or reconnect folders\n\n## Where the current contract still fragments\n\nThe problem is not that Resilio hides the ingredients.\nThe problem is that it still does not produce one first-class, case-scoped **predecessor authority retirement and exclusive successor control** object.\n\nToday an operator can often infer only weaker truths such as:\n\n- the successor world exists and can be found through newer links or keys\n- some predecessor handles were rotated or replaced\n- some peers were re-shared or relinked\n- some devices were unlinked locally, but other devices could not be remotely unlinked\n- some remote peers may still retain bytes, keys, or copied links outside the linked-identity boundary\n- a Standard-folder cohort with the old key may still be live and mutually syncing even after one actor rotates away\n- a stolen or compromised device may force a rebuild, but there is still no single page that says which predecessor authorities can still act right now\n\nThose are useful clues.\nThey are not the same as an explicit answer to `can the predecessor world still write, seed, revoke, share, attract new dependents, or keep a split world alive, and has the successor become the only legitimate actor for the named slice?`\n\n## Why that matters for AnonSync\n\nAnonSync needs a stronger sentence than `the successor is legitimate` and stronger still than `the successor is the canonical pointer`.\nIt needs to support claims such as:\n\n- the successor is canonical, but the predecessor still has live write capability through an old key cohort\n- human-facing references were rebound, but a predecessor device can still act as an active controller or seed\n- the predecessor is retired for one governed slice, while ungoverned remotes remain live and can still republish or mutate state\n- a successor world inherited standing, yet split-world exclusivity is blocked because the predecessor still has unresolved actuation lanes\n- the strongest honest sentence is `successor canonical, predecessor authority not fully extinguished`, not because discovery failed but because control retirement is a separate problem from pointer rebinding\n\nAnonSync therefore needs first-class objects for **predecessor actor set, live predecessor capability, authority class, revocation reach, split-world status, quarantine posture, successor exclusivity scope, and blocked stronger control sentence** rather than leaving operators to reconstruct control truth from key rotation rules, folder-type differences, unlink limits, remote-retention notes, copied links, or stolen-device reset recipes.\n\n## Non-clone conclusion\n\nBorrow the candor.\nDo not clone the contract shape.\n\nResilio's current docs still answer the key question — `can the old world still act, and is the successor now the only legitimate controller for the intended slice?` — only by making the operator combine several partially overlapping mechanics:\n\n- Standard-key continuation after one peer rotates away\n- folder-type-specific revoke authority and permission mutation rules\n- inability to remotely unlink other devices\n- linked-identity removal that may still leave unlinked remotes live\n- copied link and single-file forwarding beyond governance\n- catastrophic reset guidance for stolen devices\n- service-user storage forks that create distinct worlds requiring re-share or reconnect\n- architectural statements that Resilio itself cannot block or remove other peers' content or distribution\n\nThat diffusion is exactly what AnonSync should avoid.\n\n## Design consequence for AnonSync\n\nAnonSync should model **predecessor authority retirement and exclusive successor control** directly.\nIts interface family should let the product separate at least these truths:\n\n- successor valid, predecessor authority unreviewed\n- successor canonical, predecessor handles rebound, predecessor actuation still possible\n- predecessor writes blocked for named slice only\n- predecessor sharing blocked, predecessor seeding still possible\n- predecessor revocation authority removed, predecessor bytes still live off-world\n- split-world active\n- predecessor quarantined for named slice only\n- successor exclusive controller for named slice only\n- broader universal exclusivity blocked\n\nThat is why this revision adds five more first-class pages:\n**Remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement contract sheet**, **predecessor-authority-retirement review**, **predecessor-authority-retirement proof**, **predecessor-authority-retirement timeline**, and **predecessor-authority-retirement lineage receipt**.\n",
'docs/2003-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-contract-sheet-page-live-predecessor-capability-exclusive-successor-control-and-quarantine-budget-interface-spec.md': '# Remedy-hardening-attestation predecessor authority retirement contract sheet page — live predecessor capability, exclusive successor control, and quarantine budget\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page is the compact contract for deciding whether a successor world that is already legitimate and discoverable has also become the only actor that may still control, mutate, publish, seed, or revoke for the named slice.\nIt exists so the product can distinguish `successor legitimate`, `successor canonical`, `predecessor still active`, `predecessor quarantined for named slice`, `exclusive successor control for named slice`, and `broader universal exclusivity still blocked`.\n\n## Core fields\n\n- predecessor-authority-retirement identifier\n- source successor-reference-rebinding receipt identifier\n- predecessor-world identifier\n- successor-world identifier\n- governed slice identifier\n- predecessor actor family under review\n- predecessor actor inventory\n- predecessor live capability class\n- predecessor authority surface set\n- successor exclusive-control target set\n- authority rulebook version\n- live split-world status\n- predecessor write capability status\n- predecessor share capability status\n- predecessor revoke capability status\n- predecessor seed or serve capability status\n- predecessor discovery or intake capability status\n- predecessor human-trust carryover status\n- predecessor copied-handle actuation status\n- predecessor off-world action status\n- quarantine scope and posture\n- disablement or expiry evidence set\n- successor exclusivity class\n- highest currently safe exclusivity sentence\n- strongest blocked stronger sentence\n- next fact that upgrades retirement standing now\n- next fact that collapses retirement standing now\n\n## Predecessor live capability classes\n\nThe page must model at least these distinct classes:\n\n- predecessor capability unreviewed\n- predecessor known present, live capability unknown\n- predecessor can still write or mutate\n- predecessor can still share or admit dependents\n- predecessor can still seed, serve, or relay bytes\n- predecessor can still revoke or interfere\n- predecessor can still attract dependents through copied handles\n- predecessor disabled for named surface only\n- predecessor quarantined for named slice only\n- predecessor actuation extinguished for named slice only\n- broader universal retirement blocked\n\n## Authority surface types\n\nThe page must preserve at least these distinct surfaces:\n\n- write or delete surface\n- rename or replace surface\n- permission or membership surface\n- share or invite surface\n- key or handle distribution surface\n- read, seed, or serve surface\n- notification or publication surface\n- reconnect or rejoin surface\n- copied-off-world handle surface\n- unknown historical authority surface\n\n## Successor exclusivity classes\n\nThe page must support at least these classes:\n\n- successor legitimate, exclusivity unreviewed\n- successor canonical, predecessor still active\n- successor exclusive for internal governed slice only\n- successor exclusive for write surface only\n- successor exclusive for publication surface only\n- predecessor quarantined but off-world authority unresolved\n- split-world still active\n- predecessor extinguished for named slice only\n- broader universal exclusivity blocked\n\n## Fixed rendering order\n\nEvery predecessor-authority-retirement contract sheet must render the same sections in the same order:\n\n1. **Strongest currently safe exclusivity sentence**\n2. **Predecessor actor set and live capability inventory**\n3. **Quarantine posture, disablement evidence, and split-world state**\n4. **Successor exclusive-control scope and blocked stronger sentence**\n5. **Next evidence that upgrades or collapses retirement standing**\n\n## Minimum required comparisons\n\nThe page must force explicit comparison between:\n\n- successor discoverability and successor exclusivity\n- stale handle retirement and live predecessor capability\n- local unlink or removal and remote actuation survival\n- key rotation and old-key cohort survival\n- write disablement and share disablement\n- named-slice quarantine and universal retirement\n\n## Hard rules\n\nThe page must never silently upgrade:\n\n- `successor canonical` into `predecessor cannot still act`\n- `old handles rebound` into `old authorities extinguished`\n- `one peer was rotated` into `old-key cohort dead`\n- `one device was unlinked` into `all predecessor devices disabled`\n- `linked-identity cleanup done` into `off-world remotes cannot still publish or serve`\n- `stolen-device reset initiated` into `exclusive successor control already proved`\n',
'docs/2004-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-review-page-can-the-predecessor-still-act-and-is-the-successor-now-the-only-legitimate-controller-interface-spec.md': '# Remedy-hardening-attestation predecessor authority retirement review page — can the predecessor still act and is the successor now the only legitimate controller?\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page is the operator-facing review that answers the practical aftermath question after successor legitimacy and successor-pointer rebinding are already understood: even if the successor may inherit standing and be the canonical place to go, can the predecessor world still act, and has the successor actually become the only legitimate controller for the named slice?\n\n## Primary review prompts\n\nThe review must answer these prompts in order:\n\n1. **Which successor-reference-rebinding receipt is the starting basis for this retirement review?**\n2. **Which predecessor actor families are in scope: devices, peers, old-key cohorts, old-link recipients, unlinked remotes, copied exports, service-world remnants, or manually rebuilt instances?**\n3. **Which authority surfaces matter here: write, delete, replace, share, revoke, seed, serve, reconnect, or attract new dependents?**\n4. **What concrete evidence shows a predecessor actor is disabled, expired, quarantined, or still live?**\n5. **What split-world or off-world actuation lanes remain unresolved even if the successor is already canonical?**\n6. **What is the strongest predecessor-retirement sentence the product may honestly publish now?**\n\n## Review sections\n\n### 1. Starting-basis board\n\nShow:\n\n- source successor-reference-rebinding receipt\n- predecessor world identifier\n- successor world identifier\n- strongest honest rebinding sentence before retirement review\n- named governed slice\n\n### 2. Predecessor-actor board\n\nShow:\n\n- predecessor devices or peers still known\n- predecessor old-key cohorts still known\n- predecessor copied-link or copied-key cohorts still plausible\n- predecessor unlinked-remote exposure\n- predecessor service-world or storage-world remnants\n\n### 3. Live-capability board\n\nShow:\n\n- can predecessor still write or delete\n- can predecessor still rename or replace\n- can predecessor still share or invite\n- can predecessor still revoke or interfere\n- can predecessor still serve or seed bytes\n- can predecessor still attract new dependents through stale handles\n\n### 4. Quarantine and disablement board\n\nShow:\n\n- what was explicitly disabled or expired\n- what was merely forgotten locally\n- what was quarantined for named slice only\n- what remains outside governance\n- whether split-world control is still active\n\n### 5. Sentence chooser\n\nThe review must output one and only one primary sentence class such as:\n\n- successor legitimate, predecessor authority unreviewed\n- successor canonical, predecessor still active\n- predecessor write capability blocked for named slice only\n- predecessor sharing blocked, serving still unresolved\n- predecessor quarantined for named slice only\n- successor exclusive controller for named slice only\n- off-world predecessor actuation unresolved, universal exclusivity blocked\n- predecessor actuation extinguished for named slice only, broader stronger control claims blocked\n\n## Hard rules\n\nThe review must never let an operator hide:\n\n- old-key survival behind `rotated`\n- unlinked remotes behind `removed from my devices`\n- copied-off-world handles behind `canonical pointer published`\n- live predecessor seeding behind `new world is legitimate`\n- split-world activity behind `everyone should use the successor now`\n',
'docs/2005-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-proof-page-old-world-capability-quarantine-and-exclusivity-ceiling-interface-spec.md': '# Remedy-hardening-attestation predecessor authority retirement proof page — old-world capability, quarantine, and exclusivity ceiling\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page is the proof-facing object for showing whether the predecessor world can still act and what ceiling therefore applies to any stronger `exclusive successor control` sentence.\nIt exists so the product can preserve actual retirement evidence instead of collapsing rebinding, resets, and local cleanup into overclaims.\n\n## Required proof bundles\n\nEvery proof page must preserve these bundles:\n\n### 1. Source-basis bundle\n\n- source successor-reference-rebinding receipt\n- governing rulebook version\n- predecessor world and successor world identifiers\n- governed slice identifier\n\n### 2. Predecessor-capability bundle\n\n- evidence predecessor can or cannot still write\n- evidence predecessor can or cannot still share or invite\n- evidence predecessor can or cannot still revoke or interfere\n- evidence predecessor can or cannot still seed, serve, or relay\n- evidence predecessor can or cannot still attract new dependents\n\n### 3. Disablement bundle\n\n- key rotation evidence\n- expiration or unlink evidence\n- share removal or permission-lowering evidence\n- explicit disable or revoke evidence\n- rebuild, reset, or identity-regeneration evidence\n- service-world or storage-world fork evidence\n\n### 4. Quarantine bundle\n\n- named-slice quarantine controls\n- excluded surfaces still unresolved\n- off-world or ungoverned authority exposure\n- split-world continuation markers\n\n### 5. Ceiling bundle\n\n- highest justified retirement sentence\n- specific missing fact that blocks broader exclusivity\n- contradictory evidence that would collapse current standing\n\n## Proof outputs\n\nThe page must output at least:\n\n- predecessor live capability assessment\n- named-slice retirement assessment\n- successor exclusivity assessment\n- split-world activity assessment\n- off-world authority ceiling\n- blocked stronger control sentence\n\n## Strong proof classes\n\nThe page must distinguish at least these proof classes:\n\n- no reliable predecessor capability evidence\n- disablement evidence present, capability still inferential\n- named surface disabled only\n- named slice quarantined only\n- predecessor actuation extinguished for named slice only\n- broader universal retirement not proved\n- contradictory evidence implies split-world still active\n\n## Contradiction triggers\n\nThe proof page must visibly downgrade if any of these appear:\n\n- old-key peers continue syncing\n- a predecessor device cannot be remotely unlinked\n- remote non-linked devices may still hold and serve bytes\n- copied links or recipients remain outside governance\n- a service-world fork or rebuilt instance still behaves like an independent live actor\n- any stale handle still admits or routes traffic to predecessor control\n\n## Hard rules\n\nThe proof page must never let:\n\n- key rotation evidence impersonate full predecessor retirement\n- local unlink evidence impersonate remote disablement\n- reference tombstoning impersonate live capability extinction\n- successor inheritance evidence impersonate exclusive successor control\n- named-slice quarantine impersonate universal world extinguishment\n',
'docs/2006-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-timeline-page-disable-expire-revoke-unlink-quarantine-and-extinguish-events-interface-spec.md': '# Remedy-hardening-attestation predecessor authority retirement timeline page — disable, expire, revoke, unlink, quarantine, and extinguish events\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page is the time-ordered event view for how predecessor authority is supposed to die, shrink, or persist after a successor world becomes legitimate and discoverable.\nIt exists so the product can separate `new world stood up`, `old references moved`, `old actors still alive`, `quarantine imposed`, and `exclusive successor control proved`.\n\n## Required event types\n\nThe timeline must preserve at least these event types:\n\n- successor legitimacy ratified\n- canonical successor pointer chosen\n- predecessor key rotated or replaced\n- predecessor handle redirected or tombstoned\n- predecessor device unlinked locally\n- predecessor device unreachable or unknown\n- predecessor peer share removed\n- predecessor permission lowered\n- predecessor owner or revoke authority withdrawn\n- predecessor copied link observed\n- predecessor off-world recipient acknowledged\n- predecessor service-world fork created\n- predecessor rebuilt instance detected\n- quarantine for named slice imposed\n- contradictory predecessor actuation observed\n- named-surface disablement confirmed\n- named-slice retirement confirmed\n- broader exclusivity claim blocked or downgraded\n\n## Mandatory timeline questions\n\nThe page must answer in order:\n\n1. **When did the successor become legitimate?**\n2. **When did discovery move to the successor?**\n3. **When were predecessor actuation lanes explicitly disabled, if ever?**\n4. **When did contradictory evidence show the predecessor was still live?**\n5. **When was quarantine imposed and for which slice or surface?**\n6. **When, if ever, did the strongest honest sentence become `successor exclusive for named slice only`?**\n\n## Event rendering rules\n\n- Every event must show whether it affects discovery only, authority only, or both.\n- Every event must show whether it is local, governed-slice, or off-world in scope.\n- Every event must show whether it upgrades, preserves, or downgrades exclusivity standing.\n- Contradiction events must remain visible even after later repair.\n\n## Hard rules\n\nThe timeline must never let:\n\n- `successor announced` erase `predecessor still acted later`\n- `device unlinked` erase `remote unlink impossible`\n- `share removed` erase `off-world copied link survives`\n- `key rotated` erase `old-key cohort remained live`\n- `quarantine imposed` erase `universal retirement still blocked`\n',
'docs/2007-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-lineage-receipt-page-old-world-retirement-successor-exclusivity-and-blocked-stronger-control-sentences-interface-spec.md': '# Remedy-hardening-attestation predecessor authority retirement lineage receipt page — old-world retirement, successor exclusivity, and blocked stronger control sentences\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis page is the compact receipt a product can carry forward after reviewing whether the predecessor world can still act.\nIt exists so downstream users can quote one durable object instead of reconstructing exclusivity from scattered resets, revokes, rotations, and unlink lore.\n\n## Receipt body\n\nEvery predecessor-authority-retirement receipt must contain:\n\n- receipt identifier\n- predecessor-authority-retirement case identifier\n- source successor-reference-rebinding receipt identifier\n- predecessor world identifier\n- successor world identifier\n- governed slice identifier\n- current predecessor live-capability class\n- current split-world status\n- current quarantine scope\n- current successor exclusivity class\n- highest honest public sentence\n- strongest blocked stronger sentence\n- specific contradiction set that blocks the stronger sentence\n- next evidence needed for upgrade\n- downgrade trigger set\n- receipt issue time\n- receipt expiry or mandatory re-review horizon\n\n## Allowed highest honest public sentences\n\nThe receipt may expose sentences such as:\n\n- successor legitimate, predecessor authority not yet reviewed\n- successor canonical, predecessor still active\n- predecessor authority reduced on named surfaces only\n- predecessor quarantined for named slice only\n- successor exclusive controller for named slice only\n- predecessor actuation extinguished for named slice only, broader universal exclusivity blocked\n- off-world predecessor authority unresolved, stronger control claims blocked\n\n## Forbidden upgrades\n\nThe receipt must never allow:\n\n- `successor exclusive controller` without a visible scope\n- `predecessor retired` without a visible surface or slice\n- `control fully transferred` when any contradiction set remains\n- `old world gone` when only discovery moved\n- `universal exclusivity` when off-world or split-world actuation remains unresolved\n\n## Receipt downgrade triggers\n\nThe receipt must automatically become stale or downgraded when:\n\n- any predecessor actor is observed writing, deleting, sharing, or serving again\n- an old-key cohort is observed still syncing\n- a copied handle is shown to admit new dependents\n- a supposedly retired device or world reappears as an active actor\n- service-world or rebuilt-instance evidence creates a fresh split-world lane\n- new off-world authority evidence appears\n',
}

README_ADD = "## Revision addendum after rev0476 — predecessor authority retirement, split-world quarantine, and exclusive successor control\n\nThis continuation archive advances the doctrine by tightening another concrete non-clone seam around **what happens after the successor world is already legitimate, already inherits the standing it is allowed to inherit, and is already the canonical place dependents are meant to go, but the product still does not own whether the predecessor world can continue to act as a live controller, writer, inviter, revoker, seed, or competing sovereign for the same slice**.\nIt does eight things in one tranche:\n\n1. Continues the archive after rev0476 with a new page family centered on what happens *after* successor-reference rebinding exists but *before* the product may honestly pretend that the predecessor world is retired and the successor is the only legitimate actor.\n2. Tightens the non-clone line again: borrow Resilio's candor about old-key continuation, Standard-vs-Advanced revoke asymmetry, inability to remotely unlink devices, remote copies that survive linked-identity removal, copied links and single-file forwarding, stolen-device reset flows, service-user storage forks, and Resilio's own inability to control or remove peers' distributed copies; refuse any contract where the operator still has to reconstruct `can the predecessor still act?` from scattered key, share, identity, reset, and storage notes.\n3. Adds one new **Resilio evaluation** document focused on why current remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement truth is still too fragmented to clone even though the ingredients are useful.\n4. Adds five new **interface specs** for remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement contract sheet, review, proof, timeline, and lineage receipt.\n5. Makes one hard product decision explicit: **successor-world inheritance legitimacy is weaker than successor-reference rebinding legitimacy, and successor-reference rebinding legitimacy is weaker than predecessor authority retirement and exclusive successor control.**\n6. Makes another hard product decision explicit: **everyone now knows the right pointer is weaker than only the right world can still act.**\n7. Makes a third hard product decision explicit: **quarantine for one named slice, surface, or governed cohort is not universal retirement, and `old references retired` is not allowed to impersonate `old sovereign extinguished`.**\n8. Packages the result as another continuation archive whose new tranche makes the `predecessor actor set / live capability / split-world status / quarantine posture / exclusivity scope / contradiction set / receipt` seam explicit in the reading order and page family.\n\nNew docs in this tranche:\n\n- `2002-resilio-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-exclusive-successor-control-and-split-world-fragmentation-evaluation.md`\n- `2003-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-contract-sheet-page-live-predecessor-capability-exclusive-successor-control-and-quarantine-budget-interface-spec.md`\n- `2004-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-review-page-can-the-predecessor-still-act-and-is-the-successor-now-the-only-legitimate-controller-interface-spec.md`\n- `2005-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-proof-page-old-world-capability-quarantine-and-exclusivity-ceiling-interface-spec.md`\n- `2006-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-timeline-page-disable-expire-revoke-unlink-quarantine-and-extinguish-events-interface-spec.md`\n- `2007-remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement-lineage-receipt-page-old-world-retirement-successor-exclusivity-and-blocked-stronger-control-sentences-interface-spec.md`\n\n"
STATUS_ADD = "## Current status shift toward predecessor authority retirement, split-world quarantine, and exclusive successor control after rev0476\n\nThe next seam after **successor reference rebinding, stale predecessor handle retirement, and canonical-pointer truth** is now explicit:\n\n- the archive can already say whether a legitimate successor exists and whether a named set of predecessor references now point to it or are tombstoned\n- it still needed to own the harder truth of **whether the predecessor world can still act**, because pointer correctness, discovery hygiene, and legitimate inheritance do not prove that the old world stopped writing, sharing, seeding, revoking, or attracting dependents\n- current Resilio docs reinforce that gap because Standard-key rotation leaves old-key peers syncing among themselves, Standard-vs-Advanced folders differ materially on revoke and permission mutation, remote devices cannot be unlinked remotely, removal from linked devices can leave unlinked remotes live, copied file links and folder links can travel further, a stolen device response is a hard reset rather than a typed retirement receipt, service-user changes can create a new storage world, and Resilio explicitly cannot remove peers' distributed copies\n\nThis pass turns that gap into a first-class product object: **the remedy-hardening attestation predecessor-authority-retirement and exclusive-successor-control case**.\n\nWhat is newly true in the archive:\n\n- **successor reference rebinding legitimacy is weaker than predecessor authority retirement and exclusive successor control**\n- **successor canonical, predecessor still active; predecessor writes blocked for named slice only; predecessor sharing blocked, serving unresolved; predecessor quarantined for named slice only; successor exclusive controller for named slice only; and universal exclusivity blocked are separate public truths**\n- **old handles retired is weaker than old actor disabled, old actor disabled on one surface is weaker than old world quarantined, and named-slice quarantine is weaker than universal retirement**\n- **key rotation, unlinks, resets, re-shares, and removal operations now degrade into evidence inputs instead of impersonating the exclusivity verdict**\n- **every serious `only the successor can still act` sentence now needs one receipt that preserves the predecessor actor set, live capability class, split-world status, quarantine scope, contradiction set, highest honest exclusivity sentence, and the blocked stronger sentence**\n\nWhat remains intentionally true:\n\n- successor legitimacy still matters\n- successor inheritance still matters\n- successor reference rebinding still matters\n- but none of those may substitute for one explicit answer about whether the predecessor world remains a live sovereign for the governed slice\n\n"
EVAL_ADD = "## Revision addendum after rev0476 — why predecessor authority retirement, split-world quarantine, and exclusive successor control now sit on the non-clone side\n\nCurrent official Resilio docs are still admirably candid that `the successor is legitimate`, `the successor is canonical`, `the old references changed`, `the old device was unlinked`, `the old key was rotated`, and `the predecessor can no longer act` are not one flat truth.\n`Key structure and flow` still says changing a Standard-folder key is not distributed automatically and that peers with the old key continue syncing with each other.\n`What's the difference between Standard and Advanced folders?` still says Standard peers can share the key they have without limitation, on-the-fly permission changes are unavailable there, and revoke access from remote peers exists only for Advanced folders.\n`User Management` still says only Owners can revoke access rights from other peers and that this permission model belongs to Advanced folders.\n`Sync Private Identity & Linking My Devices` still says you cannot remotely unlink other devices.\n`Disconnecting and Removing Folders` still says removing a folder from linked devices may still leave it available on remote devices that are not linked to your personal identity.\n`Sharing single file` still says recipients can share files further.\n`Can Resilio team see and block/remove any Sync folders?` still says Resilio cannot control link or folder distribution and cannot remove content from users' devices or peers' devices.\n`If your device is stolen` still says the serious response path is to remove shares, unlink identity if linked, remove synced data from storage, reinstall, regenerate identity, relink devices, and reshare folders.\n`Sync Service Troubleshooting on Windows` still says switching to Local System creates a new storage world with no old folders visible and requires re-add plus re-share or reconnect.\n\nThis is strong operational candor.\nIt is also exactly why AnonSync should not clone the present contract.\nOne ordinary answer to `can the predecessor still act, and is the successor now the only legitimate controller for the intended slice?` still depends on combining key-rotation semantics, folder-type authority asymmetry, unlink limits, linked-vs-unlinked remote survival, copied-link propagation, reset recipes, service-world forks, and explicit architectural non-control of peers.\n\nSo this tranche freezes a stronger replacement line: **predecessor live capability, split-world continuation, named-slice quarantine, successor exclusivity scope, contradiction set, and blocked stronger control sentence become separate modeled truths.**\n\nThat is why this revision adds five more first-class pages: **Remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement contract sheet**, **predecessor-authority-retirement review**, **predecessor-authority-retirement proof**, **predecessor-authority-retirement timeline**, and **predecessor-authority-retirement lineage receipt**.\n\n"
SOURCES_ADD = "## rev0477 source set — predecessor authority retirement, split-world quarantine, and exclusive successor control\n\nThe most load-bearing source set for this pass was:\n\n- Resilio's current `Key structure and flow` article, which still says changing a Standard-folder key is not distributed automatically and that peers with the old Key continue syncing with each other.\n- Resilio's current `What's the difference between Standard and Advanced folders?` article, which still says Standard peers can share the key they have without limitation, on-the-fly permission changes are unavailable there, and revoke access from remote peers exists only for Advanced folders.\n- Resilio's current `User Management` article, which still says only Owners can revoke access rights from other peers and that this control applies in the Advanced-folder model.\n- Resilio's current `Sync Private Identity & Linking My Devices` article, which still says devices cannot be remotely unlinked.\n- Resilio's current `Disconnecting and Removing Folders` article, which still says removing a folder from linked devices may still leave it available on remote devices not linked to the personal identity.\n- Resilio's current `Sharing single file` article, which still says recipients can share files further.\n- Resilio's current `Can Resilio team see and block/remove any Sync folders?` article, which still says Resilio cannot control distribution and cannot remove data from peers' devices.\n- Resilio's current `If your device is stolen` article, which still says the serious response path removes shares, unlinks identity if linked, removes storage data, reinstalls, regenerates identity, relinks, and reshares.\n- Resilio's current `Sync Service Troubleshooting on Windows` article, which still says switching to Local System creates a new storage world with no old folders visible and requires re-add plus re-share or reconnect.\n\nThose sources were enough to tighten the line again:\n\n- current Resilio still deserves credit for candid predecessor-retirement ingredients\n- but current Resilio still answers `can the old world still act, and is the successor now the only legitimate controller?` too diffusely\n- AnonSync should therefore prefer explicit remedy-hardening-attestation-predecessor-authority-retirement sheets, reviews, proofs, timelines, and lineage receipts over overloaded key-rotation notes, folder-type matrices, unlink warnings, share-removal guides, reset recipes, and service-world folklore\n\nPrimary sources:\n\n- Key structure and flow\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/206767810-Key-structure-and-flow\n\n- What's the difference between Standard and Advanced folders?\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/204754679-What-s-the-difference-between-Standard-and-Advanced-folders\n\n- User Management\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/205471375-User-Management\n\n- Sync Private Identity & Linking My Devices\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/205457815-Sync-Private-Identity-Linking-My-Devices\n\n- Disconnecting and Removing Folders\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/205457785-Disconnecting-and-Removing-Folders\n\n- Sharing single file\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000401010-Sharing-single-file\n\n- Can Resilio team see and block/remove any Sync folders?\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/205451105-Can-Resilio-team-see-and-block-remove-any-Sync-folders\n\n- If your device is stolen\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/204644049-If-your-device-is-stolen\n\n- Sync Service Troubleshooting on Windows\n  https://help.resilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/207724196-Sync-Service-Troubleshooting-on-Windows\n\n"

def prepend_if_missing(path: str, text: str, marker: str) -> None:
    p = ROOT / path
    old = p.read_text()
    if marker not in old:
        p.write_text(text + old)

def main() -> None:
    for rel, content in DOCS.items():
        p = ROOT / rel
        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        p.write_text(content)
    prepend_if_missing('README.md', README_ADD, 'Revision addendum after rev0476 — predecessor authority retirement')
    prepend_if_missing('docs/00-status.md', STATUS_ADD, 'status shift toward predecessor authority retirement, split-world quarantine, and exclusive successor control after rev0476')
    prepend_if_missing('docs/10-resilio-sync-evaluation.md', EVAL_ADD, 'Revision addendum after rev0476 — why predecessor authority retirement')
    prepend_if_missing('docs/sources.md', SOURCES_ADD, '## rev0477 source set — predecessor authority retirement')

if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()
